build_layer3 always emits `{feat_list},`. When pipeline.layer3 is empty, the generated select contains a bare `,` line, which is a SyntaxError. build_final_join explicitly allows an empty layer3, but this method doesn't handle it. If TemporalSpaceBuilder returns no features (for example, operators_override filters every operator out), the generated script contains `"mob",
,
)`. The whole script then fails to compile. The same thing happens in build_layer2a when layer2a is empty (`.agg(
,
)`).
